From 09f8ede8faf589b973912b3f6b5e610630515adb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 09:42:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): carry attached source hints to managed exec and
 code kernels [daveey]

The dispatcher supplies source_env to kanban_worker_client, which only submits a
claim to the owner. The real agent.managed_worker is a separate gateway child
and never inherits that environment. Reconstruct just SOURCE_PATH/COMMIT/BRANCH
from the current attached local journal at its actual Popen boundary. Validate
task/run/claim and clear stale inherited hints for unattached scratch. Retain
ordinary env=None/kwargs semantics and leave scratch cwd/artifact policy alone.

The execute_code exact allowlist also excluded those non-secret hints even
when startup and terminal had them. Admit only these three names; no board,
claim or credential grant is added.

Why not caught: source tests stopped at a custom dispatcher spawn callback;
kernel scrub tests did not compose source custody with its real child entry.
Earlier fenced-branch repair 1d9baebbd5 kept the same memory-only transport.

Proof: baseline red-3: 3 assertion failures (materialized, holder_reuse and stale
scratch). Managed overlay alone: startup/terminal pass but execute_code fails
both source cases. After allowlist: 3 passed. Expanded regression: 13 passed;
real Popen -> terminal backend and execute_code kernel, plus stale/pending/
aborted, wrong task/claim and terminal-run refusal, copied ambient env controls.
Rendezvous consumers: 73 passed. No acceptance fixture/custody/config changes.

Co-Authored-By: GPT-6.1-sol <noreply@openai.com>
